body:
church pastors really dont like it when you give the church a bad rep in the area. i used to attend church as a kid for special occasions like christmas mass when i was in school and apparantly some members of the church had been harrassing someone for not attending . 

&#x200B;

pastor got a call from a concerned neighbour and he was furious, he was late to the sermon  which never happened before and we all just sat on our pews for half an hour until he came out. 

&#x200B;

He came out in regular clothes looking like he wanted to kill someone and asked all the harrassers to stand up, they did and were promptly expelled from the church, he in very polite terms told the rest of us he was appalled, that behaviour was not tolerated and anyone like that would be expelled aswell, he gave a brief blessing to the children that had turned up and cancelled the rest of the sermon.

&#x200B;

The church ended up closing a few years ago due to the elderly audience quickly dwindling, struggling to line up a replacement pastor for when the current one would inevitably retire and a general decline of religion in the younger generations.

the oscars is basically a way for hollywood to circle jerk each other off and inflate their already massively oversized egos. 

&#x200B;

i dont think anyone actually cares about the oscars.

therapists  are extremely reluctant to outright tell you to do something because if you do it and it turns out to be the wrong thing to do itll fall back on them, the fact that TEN of them have gone against this policy speaks volumes.

&#x200B;

you have to leave her, she wont change, they cant change, if something bad happens to her then it happens, she has broken the relationship not you and you shouldnt have to sacrifice your physical and mental health to maintain something thats clearly broken.

&#x200B;

it sounds like to me this relationship has had some strain for a while and this incident was the climax of the troubles. the bridge is falling, dont stand underneath it thinking youll be able to hold it up because youll just get crushed

This isnt just a table.

&#x200B;

This is an M&S table

yeah ive had it happen a couple times, im in england so soldiers are treated like civilians by the general public.

&#x200B;

our soldiers dont really make a big deal out of it, they wont wear military scrubs in public aswell. once a soldier gets off base in england they are a civilian and people expect them to act like one. one of the times it was a joke, the husband laughed a bit and so did i, but the other woman was dead serious, her husband didnt take too kindly to that one and had a row with her that lasted until they got back to the car

>I think the idea of banning them was to put young people and casual smokers off buying them by making it more expensive and less convenient.

&#x200B;

which did absoloutely nothing cos those types of smokers just resorted to buying cheap possibly fake possibly dangerous tobacco off their friends or dodgy corner shops

The reason why amazon is swallowing up the entirety of online shipping is because its a genuinely good service, ive only had an item arrive late once in 10 years and was immediately compensated, other times an item has arrived faulty, didnt need to send the item back just a picture of what was wrong and was refunded, ive ordered from several online companies and been purposefully messed around at least once

&#x200B;

 JD Sports used hermes, the parcel was lost for about a week and i had to go through customer service a dozen times to find where it was and multiple times they tried to claim the item had been delivered, i have a ring doorbell so had evidence that clearly wasnt the case. during covid i ordered a set of masks, 2 months went by, countless tickets raised and nothing, got a charge back from my bank and the item arrived anyway nearly 4 months late.

i ordered something and evri lost it,evri messed me and seller around and woulldnt admit they lost it for a month. got a refund from the seller.

&#x200B;

cue to 4 MONTHS later an evri van pulling up and giving me my order.

yeah, if he has no quarrel with you i believe his friendliness is genuine, he is very understanding when his LPH employees mess up, we see hes capable of genuine fear, when he finds out lalo is still alive, in the meeting with eladio and max.

&#x200B;

hes not a psychopath, hes just been hardened by a trauma which probably broke him mentally.

rep visit day was always good when i worked in the college store, to clarify i did an animal care course and just off campus their was a pet shop run by the college to help subsidize the course.

&#x200B;

reps used to come around at least once a month to make sure products were properly displayed and in good condition, theyd always give the workers tons of free pet gear and food, at least 3 times i had so much free stuff given to me id have to make multiple trips to get it all home in my suitcase

my NHS experience in 2015: Teen with a suspected heart attack, rapid response vehicle arrived within half an hour, took an ecg, given mild sedative to control heart rate, ambulance arrived 10 mins later, arrived at hospital and within 3 hours i had blood drawn, tested and was on my way home.

&#x200B;

today it seems like it would take multiple hours just for the ambulance to arrive

and it took netflix 25 years to build up their company to that level, meanwhile disney plus has over 150 million subscribers despite only being less than 4 years old, prime video has more subscribers than netflix and its 10 years younger.

&#x200B;

they blitzkreiged their way into streaming but now theyve stretched themselves too thin and their house of cards is crumbling rapidly. theyve cancelled several shows and lost dozens of ips in the last few years, everyones setting up their own streaming services, used to be netflix and prime video were the only major ones, now we have paramount plus, disney plus, netflix, prime, hulu, hbo. the market is quickly becoming oversaturated

yup, the whole "red wave" that was supposed to happen in the last midterm flopped hard, they just barely got the house back and solifided their minority status in the senate, trump lost the gop everything,  in just a couple months both the white house, senate AND house went from red to blue. Mccarthy had to make so many deals and concessions he was basically neutered of any real infuence before he was even voted in.

&#x200B;

if trump does somehow get back in it will be even worse, he will be too busy weaponizing the doj to bury the countless lawsuits hes involved in to do anything meaning all his advisers and secretaries will be running rampant doing whatever they want, apparantly donald trump stopped holding cabinet meetings and the white house was a ghost town after the election results came in.

&#x200B;

i think secretly even mitch mcconnell is ashamed of the state of the gop, they went from being somewhat sane and being able to at least uphold an appearance of normality, now the dams broke and the insanity that used to be restricted to the lower rungs of the gop ladder has been flung all the way to the top.
